{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xcnt45hToDSnqnnT2VGAqE","type":"tool_result","content":"227:- `view.screenDirToGround(dx, dy)`: a direction the player pushed on screen (x right, y down) -> normalized ground direction\n228:- `view.set(yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1)`: change the angles and scale in place (game.setView and rotateView use their own copies); returns the view\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (men\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n492:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom)\n494:- `game.rotateView(deg)` †: turn the camera around the vertical axis in ground views: game.rotateView(45) (degrees). Side views never turn\n498:- `game.setZoom(z)` †: camera zoom on top of the view: game.setZoom(1.5) (.5 .. 3), the game's own; where the scene lets the player zoom (camera.zoom), theirs multiplies it (game.zoom is the two together). Characters, maps, props, particles and lights are drawn by code, so they re-rasterize cris\n557:- `game.yaw = 0` †: its turn in degrees on top of the view (rotateView)\n558:- `game.zoom = 1` †: the camera's zoom now (1 = as the view is): the game's (setZoom, a scene's camera.start) times the player's (settings.zoom: the wheel, a pinch), within the scene's camera.zoom range\n618:- `saves.any` †: is there any save to load (a title's Continue)?\n619:- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)\n620:- `saves.copy(from, to)` †: copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty\n621:- `saves.erase(slot)` †: erase a slot\n622:- `saves.get(slot)` †: a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer: true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, place, level, time, at (the date saved), version }\n623:- `saves.latest()` †: the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it)\n624:- `saves.list()` †: every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows)\n625:- `saves.load(slot)` †: load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from a newer version\n626:- `saves.save(slot, o)` †: save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocked tells), false when there was nothing to save\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n628:- `saves.blocked = false` †: storage refused a save (they last for the visit)\n629:- `saves.canSave = true` †: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points)\n630:- `saves.game` †: its game\n631:- `saves.migrate` †: an older version's data brought up to this one (or null: kept as it is)\n632:- `saves.played = 0` †: seconds played in the game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load\n633:- `saves.read` †: what a load does with { data, place, level, time, slot }\n634:- `saves.slots` †: how many slots besides the autosave (3)\n635:- `saves.version` †: the game's version of its data (1), saved with each save\n636:- `saves.write` †: what a save holds ({ data, place, level })","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82f305e6-f719-4e49-881f-e498d001a34b","uuid":"fa554b0f-24a0-4041-8bca-b5398305f3ea","timestamp":"2026-11-04T05:15:05.120Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"227:- `view.screenDirToGround(dx, dy)`: a direction the player pushed on screen (x right, y down) -> normalized ground direction\n228:- `view.set(yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1)`: change the angles and scale in place (game.setView and rotateView use their own copies); returns the view\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (men\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n492:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom)\n494:- `game.rotateView(deg)` †: turn the camera around the vertical axis in ground views: game.rotateView(45) (degrees). Side views never turn\n498:- `game.setZoom(z)` †: camera zoom on top of the view: game.setZoom(1.5) (.5 .. 3), the game's own; where the scene lets the player zoom (camera.zoom), theirs multiplies it (game.zoom is the two together). Characters, maps, props, particles and lights are drawn by code, so they re-rasterize cris\n557:- `game.yaw = 0` †: its turn in degrees on top of the view (rotateView)\n558:- `game.zoom = 1` †: the camera's zoom now (1 = as the view is): the game's (setZoom, a scene's camera.start) times the player's (settings.zoom: the wheel, a pinch), within the scene's camera.zoom range\n618:- `saves.any` †: is there any save to load (a title's Continue)?\n619:- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)\n620:- `saves.copy(from, to)` †: copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty\n621:- `saves.erase(slot)` †: erase a slot\n622:- `saves.get(slot)` †: a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer: true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, place, level, time, at (the date saved), version }\n623:- `saves.latest()` †: the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it)\n624:- `saves.list()` †: every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows)\n625:- `saves.load(slot)` †: load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from a newer version\n626:- `saves.save(slot, o)` †: save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocked tells), false when there was nothing to save\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n628:- `saves.blocked = false` †: storage refused a save (they last for the visit)\n629:- `saves.canSave = true` †: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points)\n630:- `saves.game` †: its game\n631:- `saves.migrate` †: an older version's data brought up to this one (or null: kept as it is)\n632:- `saves.played = 0` †: seconds played in the game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load\n633:- `saves.read` †: what a load does with { data, place, level, time, slot }\n634:- `saves.slots` †: how many slots besides the autosave (3)\n635:- `saves.version` †: the game's version of its data (1), saved with each save\n636:- `saves.write` †: what a save holds ({ data, place, level })","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Xcnt45hToDSnqnnT2VGAqE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
