{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018wJtKRdhwANJomhk9FMRU4","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nsrc/10-world.js:220\nsrc/00-core.js:206\nsrc/30-ui.js:208\nsrc/40-draw.js:98\nsrc/20-play.js:607\nsrc/99-main.js:83\nsrc/35-scenes.js:309\nsrc/98-report.js:8","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82f305e6-f719-4e49-881f-e498d001a34b","uuid":"b6d0a7c5-d8c0-4a2c-ae5a-26625f8623e2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T05:29:56.247Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"---\nsrc/10-world.js:220\nsrc/00-core.js:206\nsrc/30-ui.js:208\nsrc/40-draw.js:98\nsrc/20-play.js:607\nsrc/99-main.js:83\nsrc/35-scenes.js:309\nsrc/98-report.js:8","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018wJtKRdhwANJomhk9FMRU4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghLYY19MDS5FkWP6B29W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XLQep5JVSzMFqLRSET7Epy","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-221326__x5b1962/work/DragonQuiltBuilders-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-221326/src/98-report.js","content":"// The About & Credits pages: the source information, the feedback sections, and what this demo leaves out. The same\n// answers are in exit-interview.json beside the game's HTML file.\n(() => {\nconst DQ = globalThis.DQ;\nDQ.REPORT_PAGES = [\n  { title: 'Source Information', lines: [\n    'Date: 2026-11-03 22:13:26',\n    'Source: Dragon Quest Builders',\n    'Plan: PLAN.md',\n    'Genre: sandbox action RPG with block building, crafting, town building, a siege and a boss.',\n    'Perspective: third-person isometric (the camera turns in quarter steps; a three-quarter view is one key away).',\n    'Tech: my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (handoff), plain JavaScript, Canvas 2D. AI Hub client session.js 1.4.0, unmodified.',\n    'Art direction: a patchwork quilt. Blocks are fabric patches with stitched seams and shaded colour, drawn at PS1 resolution.',\n    'Animation: the engine\\'s own rigs and sword moves, and its blob squash. No new animations were made.',\n    'Audio: music, effects and voices written in code. The voices are Animalese-style blips, one voice per speaker.',\n    'Online: AI Hub parallel mode, the Quilting Bee (a three-minute round, one to four players).',\n    'Testing: headless scripted tests, the engine\\'s browser checker, and the AI Hub harness.',\n    'Research: none beyond the engine\\'s API card and the AI Hub protocol.',\n    'Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium headless via Playwright.',\n    'Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium.',\n    'Usage: unknown.',\n  ] },\n  { title: 'Testing Feedback', lines: [\n    'Issues found: about 12 in the game, plus several mistakes in my own tests.',\n    'Critical: 2. Blocks were drawn over the Builder (a depth anchor in the wrong units). A hub session did not open into the round.',\n    'Most helpful: a browser screenshot at two Builder positions. The headless checks could not show the depth bug.',\n    'Least helpful: the engine checker\\'s colour-count notes. They suit a bright scene, not a dim block world at night.',\n  ] },\n  { title: 'Engine Feedback', lines: [\n    'Liked most: the rigs with E.MOVES and E.Attack, and the standard pause, settings, dialog and menus.',\n    'Stuck or guessed wrong: r.queue takes world units, and I first passed cell numbers. I also guessed at E.font options.',\n    'Built myself: the voxel world. Storage, step-up collision, block rays, room detection and per-block drawing.',\n    'Hardest: stacking blocks inside the isometric depth-sorted draw. The TileMap is a heightmap with one wall per cell.',\n    'Changes to the engine: none. my-3d2dge.js is untouched.',\n    'One change I would make: put the units and anchor in the r.queue and r.box names, and add stacked voxel columns.',\n  ] },\n  { title: 'Prompt Feedback', lines: [\n    'Liked most: the deliverable names, the no-subagent rule, the test-output rule and the hub link.',\n    'Confusing: PLAN.md names another file and timestamp. TASK.md wins, but the plan is 1,674 lines and it is hard to know what to keep.',\n    'Hardest: fitting the plan into one session. A voxel world drawn in isometric depth order takes most of the time.',\n    'Change: name the file once, say which file wins, and give a smaller minimum demo to aim for.',\n  ] },\n  { title: 'Controls and scope', lines: [\n    'Controller: left stick walks, Cross jumps, Square breaks and strikes, Circle dodges, Triangle uses and talks, R2 places, L1 and R1 turn the camera, C or Back crafts. Glyphs follow the device used last; Settings shows Xbox letters.',\n    'Keyboard: WASD walk, Space jump, J or X break, E place, F use, C craft, I satchel, Q and R turn, B changes view, 1 to 8 pick a slot.',\n    'Mouse: aims at the ground under the pointer, click breaks or strikes, right click places.',\n    'Left out of this demo: blueprints and Patterns, residents who help build, Bobbin Ballistas and portals, shared-world co-op, and voice acting.',\n  ] },\n];\n})();\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2100,"cache_read_input_tokens":320081,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2100},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82f305e6-f719-4e49-881f-e498d001a34b","uuid":"fccca25c-1955-4124-aae0-7bce5410b8df","timestamp":"2026-11-04T05:30:03.681Z","request_id":"req_011CghLYXiXZtVcBsCrpnX1N","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XLQep5JVSzMFqLRSET7Epy":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-221326__x5b1962/work/DragonQuiltBuilders-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-221326/src/98-report.js","content":"// The About & Credits pages: the source information, the feedback sections, and what this demo leaves out. The same\n// answers are in exit-interview.json beside the game's HTML file.\n(() => {\nconst DQ = globalThis.DQ;\nDQ.REPORT_PAGES = [\n  { title: 'Source Information', lines: [\n    'Date: 2026-11-03 22:13:26',\n    'Source: Dragon Quest Builders',\n    'Plan: PLAN.md',\n    'Genre: sandbox action RPG with block building, crafting, town building, a siege and a boss.',\n    'Perspective: third-person isometric (the camera turns in quarter steps; a three-quarter view is one key away).',\n    'Tech: my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (handoff), plain JavaScript, Canvas 2D. AI Hub client session.js 1.4.0, unmodified.',\n    'Art direction: a patchwork quilt. Blocks are fabric patches with stitched seams and shaded colour, drawn at PS1 resolution.',\n    'Animation: the engine\\'s own rigs and sword moves, and its blob squash. No new animations were made.',\n    'Audio: music, effects and voices written in code. The voices are Animalese-style blips, one voice per speaker.',\n    'Online: AI Hub parallel mode, the Quilting Bee (a three-minute round, one to four players).',\n    'Testing: headless scripted tests, the engine\\'s browser checker, and the AI Hub harness.',\n    'Research: none beyond the engine\\'s API card and the AI Hub protocol.',\n    'Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium headless via Playwright.',\n    'Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium.',\n    'Usage: unknown.',\n  ] },\n  { title: 'Testing Feedback', lines: [\n    'Issues found: about 12 in the game, plus several mistakes in my own tests.',\n    'Critical: 2. Blocks were drawn over the Builder (a depth anchor in the wrong units). A hub session did not open into the round.',\n    'Most helpful: a browser screenshot at two Builder positions. The headless checks could not show the depth bug.',\n    'Least helpful: the engine checker\\'s colour-count notes. They suit a bright scene, not a dim block world at night.',\n  ] },\n  { title: 'Engine Feedback', lines: [\n    'Liked most: the rigs with E.MOVES and E.Attack, and the standard pause, settings, dialog and menus.',\n    'Stuck or guessed wrong: r.queue takes world units, and I first passed cell numbers. I also guessed at E.font options.',\n    'Built myself: the voxel world. Storage, step-up collision, block rays, room detection and per-block drawing.',\n    'Hardest: stacking blocks inside the isometric depth-sorted draw. The TileMap is a heightmap with one wall per cell.',\n    'Changes to the engine: none. my-3d2dge.js is untouched.',\n    'One change I would make: put the units and anchor in the r.queue and r.box names, and add stacked voxel columns.',\n  ] },\n  { title: 'Prompt Feedback', lines: [\n    'Liked most: the deliverable names, the no-subagent rule, the test-output rule and the hub link.',\n    'Confusing: PLAN.md names another file and timestamp. TASK.md wins, but the plan is 1,674 lines and it is hard to know what to keep.',\n    'Hardest: fitting the plan into one session. A voxel world drawn in isometric depth order takes most of the time.',\n    'Change: name the file once, say which file wins, and give a smaller minimum demo to aim for.',\n  ] },\n  { title: 'Controls and scope', lines: [\n    'Controller: left stick walks, Cross jumps, Square breaks and strikes, Circle dodges, Triangle uses and talks, R2 places, L1 and R1 turn the camera, C or Back crafts. Glyphs follow the device used last; Settings shows Xbox letters.',\n    'Keyboard: WASD walk, Space jump, J or X break, E place, F use, C craft, I satchel, Q and R turn, B changes view, 1 to 8 pick a slot.',\n    'Mouse: aims at the ground under the pointer, click breaks or strikes, right click places.',\n    'Left out of this demo: blueprints and Patterns, residents who help build, Bobbin Ballistas and portals, shared-world co-op, and voice acting.',\n  ] },\n];\n})();\n"}}}
