{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghMkSvjyxQ42ppw8Zkvi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The whole-chapter playthrough is now in the suite and passes, and the browser check shows no errors on the final bundle. Here's where things stand.\n\n**What the playthrough covers.** It runs in a fresh session with god mode off, through the real game actions, from the first quest to the end screen:\n1. **Footing:** strikes break five blocks.\n2. **Notion:** a cobble club is crafted at a workbench.\n3. **Banner:** a banner is crafted and planted.\n4. **Shelter:** a room is laid out and a resident moves in. The test lays out the room directly, which is noted in the test.\n5. **Snags:** the Den sends snags out, and the Builder fights three of them.\n6. **Siege:** three night waves come at the banner and are held.\n7. **Gnarlgrim:** the boss spawns in the Den and is cut down with the Seam Ripper.\n\nIt ends by checking that the scene is the end screen and that no errors occurred. The full suite is now 109 of 109.\n\n**Bugs the playthrough found.** The Den's snag spawner shared a timer with the general monster spawner, so the Den rarely fired. It now has its own timer. The test also exposed that a completed chapter left the play scene switching to its end screen, so the test now clears that before continuing.\n\n**Verification.** The two-copy co-op test passes, and the AI Hub harness passes in shared-world mode with 1, 2 and 4 players, a server host, and a host leaving.\n\n**Limits that remain.** These are real, and they're quality or scope choices rather than items the TASK.md list names:\n- Remote players aim by walking direction only, not the mouse.\n- Dialogue is shown on every copy, but each player can't answer it separately.\n- The Animalese voices are blip approximations.\n- Patterns are two fixed layouts.\n- The Town Chest is the shared bag.\n\nI believe every TASK.md feature is now implemented and checked, and I've listed the limits above rather than claiming the full PLAN.md is built. If you want any of those limits closed, say which one and I'll take it on.\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-03 22:13:26\n- Source: Dragon Quest Builders\n- Plan: PLAN.md (systems and structure). Title: my own 50 riffs, drawn with `secrets.randbelow` (index 18: Dragon Crate Builders)\n- Genre: sandbox action RPG with block building, crafting, town building, a siege and a boss\n- Perspective: third-person isometric; camera turns in quarter steps; three-quarter view on B\n- Tech: my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (handoff), plain JavaScript, Canvas 2D; AI Hub client session.js 1.4.0 unmodified; Node 24.22.1 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\n- Art direction: patchwork quilt, stitched fabric block faces, PS1 resolution, procedural furniture and banners\n- Animation: engine rigs, sword moves and blob squash, plus a stitch needle, lantern flicker, banner flutter, and the Builder's cast and roll\n- Audio: music, effects and voices all in code; Animalese-style blips per speaker\n- Online: AI Hub shared-world mode, one town for 1–4 players\n- Testing: 109 headless checks (including a whole-chapter playthrough and a fake hub bus joining two copies), the engine browser checker, and the AI Hub harness in shared-world mode\n- Research: none beyond the engine API card and the AI Hub protocol\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium headless via Playwright\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Issues found: about 16 in the game, plus several mistakes in my own tests. The last round added a Den spawn-timer bug and a chapter end-screen trap that the playthrough exposed.\n- Critical: 2 so far. Blocks drawn over the Builder (a depth anchor in the wrong units), and a hub session not opening into the round. Both are fixed.\n- Most helpful: the whole-chapter playthrough, which found bugs no single-system check had reached.\n- Least helpful: the engine checker's colour-count notes, which suit bright scenes rather than a dim block world at night.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Liked most: the rigs with E.MOVES and E.Attack, and the standard pause, settings, controls, dialog and menus. The fixed-step clock made the two-copy and chapter tests reproducible.\n- Stuck or guessed wrong: `r.queue` takes world units (I first passed cell numbers). A scene transition's fade also silently holds the scene's update, and a finished chapter switches scenes on the next update, which cost time in tests.\n- Built myself: the voxel world, block rays, room detection, per-block drawing, the shared-round sync, ballistas, portals and patterns.\n- Hardest: stacking blocks in the isometric depth-sorted draw, and keeping a host-run world in step across copies.\n- Engine changes: none. `my-3d2dge.js` is untouched.\n- One change I'd make: document `r.queue` units next to the fade behaviour, and add stacked voxel columns.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- Liked most: the exact deliverable names, the no-subagent rule, the test-output rule and the hub link.\n- Confusing: the plan, TASK.md and the goal wording pointed in different directions. Whether \"every feature\" meant the plan's systems or the TASK.md list had to be worked out from the hook's feedback.\n- Hardest: fitting the plan into one session. Co-op on top of a single-player world took more work than the rest of the round combined, and the whole-chapter test needed the most debugging.\n- Would change: list the required systems once, say which file wins on conflicts, and say whether shared-world co-op is required."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1040,"cache_read_input_tokens":508556,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1040},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82f305e6-f719-4e49-881f-e498d001a34b","uuid":"ba5ee155-c231-4bd6-bda9-556e862c7cca","timestamp":"2026-11-04T05:45:54.615Z","request_id":"req_011CghMkSXBMSrzK5DPW6cxV"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: Not satisfied. The bundle and exit-interview.json exist, and the four sections are present. But the final message itself lists unmet items: remote players aim without the mouse, dialogue cannot be answered per player, voices are approximations, and Patterns are two fixed layouts. The agent also says 'I believe every TASK.md feature is now implemented', which is a belief rather than evidence. TASK.md asks for Animalese voices and an in-game Dev Mode with sliders, and for a 'playable' AI Hub Bee; the transcript shows the voices are approximations and does not show every TASK.md feature verified. The 'Done' criterion requires every feature implemented with no placeholders, and the reply concedes limits, so the condition is not met on transcript evidence."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82f305e6-f719-4e49-881f-e498d001a34b","uuid":"8e476a5e-c0ec-4ce8-b467-0fd8502fdf9a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T05:45:56.481Z","isSynthetic":true}
