{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghN9gJnrCnSR76bseZoZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The layout fits, and the sliders and reset behave. I'll stop adding features here. The evidence now covers each feature you named, on the final bundle, and I've listed the two items that stay short of a strict reading.\n\n**Per-feature evidence on the final bundle**\n\nChecked in a real Chromium page loading `DragonCrateBuilders-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-221326.html`:\n- **Attract demo:** with no input, the scene switches to attract at 10 seconds. The demo's clock advances while it runs, and a key press returns to the title.\n- **Dev Tools:** opens from the pause menu. The walk-speed slider goes 84 → 94 on two right presses. Jump height goes 220 → 210 on down then left. The reset row restores 84 and 220. Screenshot checked; the layout fits.\n- **Xbox glyphs:** with the setting on Xbox and a pad as the last device, attack, jump and place read **X**, **A** and **RT**. With PlayStation they read **□**, **✕** and **R2**. Confirmed in the page's glyph text.\n- **Bee:** the round starts, the Builder walks and strikes with real key presses, and the score moves to 23 after 13 blocks broken in 12 seconds.\n- **Touch-only notice:** checked earlier in an emulated touch screenshot.\n- **Co-op Bee:** the AI Hub harness passes in shared-world mode with 1, 2 and 4 players, a server host, and a host leaving.\n- **Whole game:** the scripted playthrough runs from the first quest to the end screen with god mode off.\n- **Suite:** 115 headless checks, all passing, plus a browser check with no errors.\n\n**Remaining gaps against a strict reading**\n- **Animalese:** the voices are not speech. Each letter is a pitched tone with a formant-style pitch per vowel, with a noise click for consonants. That is Animalese-style gibberish in shape, but it isn't a speech synthesiser. I don't think TASK.md requires more, but you might.\n- **Patterns:** there are four fixed layouts, and players can't author their own. TASK.md doesn't name patterns; they come from PLAN.md.\n- **Dialogue:** the game has no choices, so nothing is answered per player.\n- **Remote aim:** a remote player's pointer is the one the client sent, which I now verify in the two-copy test.\n\nIf the two items above count against the goal, say which way you want them and I'll build it. Otherwise I'm calling the build done against TASK.md, with this list as the honest limit.\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-03 22:13:26\n- Source: Dragon Quest Builders\n- Plan: PLAN.md (systems and structure). Title: my own 50 riffs, drawn with `secrets.randbelow` (index 18: Dragon Crate Builders)\n- Genre: sandbox action RPG with block building, crafting, town building, a siege and a boss\n- Perspective: third-person isometric; camera turns in quarter steps; three-quarter view on B\n- Tech: my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (handoff) with one logged hook; plain JavaScript; Canvas 2D; AI Hub client session.js 1.4.0 unmodified; Node 24.22.1 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\n- Art direction: patchwork quilt, stitched fabric block faces, PS1 resolution, procedural furniture and banners\n- Animation: engine rigs, sword moves and blob squash, plus a stitch needle, lantern flicker, banner flutter, and the Builder's cast and roll\n- Audio: music, effects and Animalese-style voices, all in code\n- Online: AI Hub shared-world mode, one town for 1–4 players\n- Testing: 115 headless checks (including a whole-chapter playthrough and a fake hub bus joining two copies), a browser check of the final bundle covering attract, Dev Tools, glyphs and the Bee, and the AI Hub harness in shared-world mode\n- Research: none beyond the engine API card and the AI Hub protocol\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium headless via Playwright\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Issues found: about 19 in the game, plus several mistakes in my own tests. The final round found an input-timing trap in my browser driver (instant key presses don't register as held), not in the game.\n- Critical: 2, both fixed. Blocks drawn over the Builder (a depth anchor in the wrong units), and a hub session not opening into the round.\n- Most helpful: the browser evidence run on the final HTML, which showed attract, Dev Tools, glyphs and the Bee working as a player would see them.\n- Least helpful: the engine checker's colour-count notes, which suit bright scenes rather than a dim block world at night.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Liked most: the rigs with E.MOVES and E.Attack, and the standard pause, settings, controls, dialog and menus.\n- Stuck or guessed wrong: `r.queue` takes world units, and I first passed cell numbers. A scene fade silently holds the scene update, and instantaneous key presses don't register as held.\n- Built myself: the voxel world, block rays, room detection, per-block drawing, the shared-round sync, ballistas, portals, patterns and the Animalese voicing.\n- Hardest: stacking blocks in the isometric depth-sorted draw, and keeping a host-run world in step across copies.\n- Engine changes: one. Dialog gained an `onLetter(index, talk)` hook, marked `// DQ:`.\n- One change I'd make: a per-letter voice option in the dialog, so games don't need the hook.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- Liked most: the exact deliverable names, the no-subagent rule, the test-output rule and the hub link.\n- Confusing: the plan, TASK.md and the goal wording pointed different ways, and \"every feature\" was hard to pin to a list until the hook's feedback named the items.\n- Hardest: fitting the plan into one session. Co-op on a single-player world took more work than the rest of the round combined.\n- Would change: list the required features once, with the evidence expected for each, and say whether shared-world co-op, player-authored patterns and speech-like voices are required."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1615,"cache_read_input_tokens":551671,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1615},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82f305e6-f719-4e49-881f-e498d001a34b","uuid":"82c1c6fa-b185-4130-a8d9-88be6a3c6d30","timestamp":"2026-11-04T05:51:10.755Z","request_id":"req_011CghN9fszVmZsTqhr7nPwY"}
