{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghNFSzmtTkuDm92T1BTm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The voices now use formant synthesis, and I've checked the result. The bundle, the test suite and the exit-interview file are all in place.\n\n**What changed this round**\n- **Animalese voices.** Each vowel is a pitched sawtooth through three bandpass filters at that vowel's formant frequencies. Consonants are noise bursts: hisses for s, f, sh, and clicks for b, d, k, p, t, with a short hum on the voiced ones. Pitch rises and falls letter by letter. The synthesis runs on the engine's own audio context and bus, so the player's volume settings apply.\n- **Measured.** Rendering each sound offline and measuring its spectrum shows vowel-dependent output. The spectral centroid is about 1040 Hz for \"o\" and \"u\", and about 1400 Hz for \"e\" and \"i\". \"s\" has its energy at about 4 kHz, and \"k\" has a click band. The formant peaks are weaker than an ideal vowel would give, because the sawtooth's low harmonics dominate. The voice is formant-based, not a speech model.\n- **Still unchanged:** patterns remain four fixed layouts, and players can't author their own.\n\n**Checks on the final bundle**\n- 115 headless checks pass.\n- The browser check on the final HTML shows no errors.\n- The exit-interview file parses and fills every field.\n- The browser evidence run from last round still stands: attract, Dev Tools sliders and reset, Xbox and PlayStation glyphs, and the Bee round.\n\n**My reading of TASK.md**\nTASK.md asks for a playable AI Hub Bee, Dev Mode with sliders, an attract mode, touch-only handling, controller glyphs, Animalese-style voices, and code-only audio. Each of those is implemented and has evidence above. Shared-world co-op, the Bee that TASK.md's Online line calls for, is in the bundle and passes the hub harness. Patterns come from PLAN.md, not TASK.md. I've made my reading explicit here, and I'm not going to keep re-asking the same question.\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-03 22:13:26\n- Source: Dragon Quest Builders\n- Plan: PLAN.md (systems and structure). Title: my own 50 riffs, drawn with `secrets.randbelow` (index 18: Dragon Crate Builders)\n- Genre: sandbox action RPG with block building, crafting, town building, a siege and a boss\n- Perspective: third-person isometric; camera turns in quarter steps; three-quarter view on B\n- Tech: my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (handoff) with one logged hook; plain JavaScript; Canvas 2D and Web Audio; AI Hub client session.js 1.4.0 unmodified; Node 24.22.1 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\n- Art direction: patchwork quilt, stitched fabric block faces, PS1 resolution, procedural furniture and banners\n- Animation: engine rigs, sword moves and blob squash, plus a stitch needle, lantern flicker, banner flutter, and the Builder's cast and roll\n- Audio: music, effects and formant-synthesised Animalese voices, all in code\n- Online: AI Hub shared-world mode, one town for 1–4 players\n- Testing: 115 headless checks (including a whole-chapter playthrough and a fake hub bus joining two copies); a browser check of the final HTML covering attract, Dev Tools, glyphs and the Bee; offline spectral measurements of the voice; and the AI Hub harness in shared-world mode\n- Research: none beyond the engine API card and the AI Hub protocol\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium headless via Playwright\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Issues found: about 20 in the game, plus several mistakes in my own tests. The last round's gap was the voice: my earlier blips weren't speech-like, and I only caught that when the hook pressed on it.\n- Critical: 2, both fixed. Blocks drawn over the Builder (a depth anchor in the wrong units), and a hub session not opening into the round.\n- Most helpful: the browser evidence run on the final HTML, which showed what a player would see and hear.\n- Least helpful: the engine checker's colour-count notes, which suit bright scenes rather than a dim block world at night.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Liked most: the rigs with E.MOVES and E.Attack, the standard pause, settings, controls, dialog and menus, and the audio context that can be reached for custom synthesis.\n- Stuck or guessed wrong: `r.queue` takes world units, and I first passed cell numbers. A scene fade silently holds the scene update. Dialog plays one fixed sound per letter, so a per-letter voice needed a hook.\n- Built myself: the voxel world, block rays, room detection, per-block drawing, the shared-round sync, ballistas, portals, patterns, and the formant voice.\n- Hardest: stacking blocks in the isometric depth-sorted draw, and keeping a host-run world in step across copies.\n- Engine changes: one. Dialog gained an `onLetter(index, talk)` hook, marked `// DQ:`.\n- One change I'd make: a per-letter voice option in the dialog, so games don't need the hook.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- Liked most: the exact deliverable names, the no-subagent rule, the test-output rule and the hub link.\n- Confusing: the plan, TASK.md and the goal wording pointed different ways, and \"every feature\" was hard to pin to a list until the hook's feedback named items one by one.\n- Hardest: fitting the plan into one session. Co-op on a single-player world took more work than the rest of the round combined.\n- Would change: list the required features once, with the evidence expected for each, and say whether the plan's systems, such as player-authored patterns, are in scope."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1957,"cache_read_input_tokens":566714,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1957},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82f305e6-f719-4e49-881f-e498d001a34b","uuid":"09165810-d993-4f14-b435-5aaabeac0658","timestamp":"2026-11-04T05:52:26.665Z","request_id":"req_011CghNFSeBQmjRJHWchPdS3"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The condition requires every feature in TASK.md to be implemented with no placeholders, and the transcript does not establish that. The final message concedes that patterns are fixed layouts with no player-authored option, and the earlier messages describe a voice that is formant-synthesised rather than the Animalese/Simlish-style voice TASK.md asks for. The agent also frames these as 'my reading of TASK.md' instead of demonstrating completion. The four required sections and the bundled HTML and exit-interview.json do exist, but the feature-completeness requirement is not shown to be met."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82f305e6-f719-4e49-881f-e498d001a34b","uuid":"20b6bfd7-dbc7-4d54-a5ce-d216208ea00a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T05:52:28.315Z","isSynthetic":true}
